  "title": "NASA’s Boeing Crew Flight Test Status News Conference – Thursday, July 25, 2024",
  "description": "On Thursday, July 25, NASA Commercial Crew Program Manager Steve Stich and Boeing vice president and commercial crew program manager Mark Nappi discuss the latest status update on the agency's Crew Flight Test, or CFT. CFT is the first flight of humans aboard Boeing's Starliner spacecraft, which carried NASA astronauts Butch Wilmore and Suni Williams to the International Space Station after launching atop ULA's Atlas V rocket on June 6, 2024.   Join NASA as we go forward to the Moon and on to Mars -- discover the latest on Earth, the Solar System and beyond with a weekly update in your inbox.  Subscribe at: https://www.nasa.gov/subscribe",
